messages:
maria: Quick FYI — small auth proxy tweak in PR #4567. Only header normalization for downstream onprem sidecar, no KMS/path changes. Planning to merge in ~2h if no security/privacy concerns.

alex: pinging @sec-bot and @dan for a quick look.

sec-bot: Automated scan complete — no secrets detected. Warning: header normalization touched; recommend manual review for egress/header-based auth logic.

dan: quick skim — change narrows header handling (drops x-legacy) but doesn't add new surface. Looks ok from authz POV. Would like privacy to confirm onprem egress behavior. @sam?

sam: I can take this — spare ~20m. Can you paste the small diff or the snippet that touches the header handling? Also confirm no new env vars or secret reads.

maria: thanks — snippet below:```js
// drop legacy header added by older clients
if (req.headers['x-legacy-client']) {
  // we intentionally ignore legacy header to avoid replay surface
  delete req.headers['x-legacy-client'];
}
proxyReq.setHeader('x-internal-user', sanitizedUser);
```
No new env vars, no KMS calls. Just normalization.

sam: LGTM — behavior is explicitly narrowing the attacker surface, not widening. Two tiny asks: add a one-line comment about why we drop `x-legacy-client` (for auditing), and add a short test that asserts header is removed in onprem integration tests. After that, happy to approve. :+1:

maria: will add comment and a small test now, then merge. Thanks all.

sec-bot: Note: post-merge canary smoke scheduled (+10m). Will alert if any auth regression metrics spike.
